  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Public bodies select on exams and interviews while software employers select on skill and projects. Both judge you by consistency and clarity.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing a plan with an end date and reviewing it honestly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and UPSC vs software engineering: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools explain topics and generate practice. Routine preparation aids are easy to get.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, integrity and accountability hold value in both. A staged path helps: now, use AI to learn and quiz; later, own decisions in your chosen field.
  </p>

